.TH CONSIGNE 1 "2026-08-10" "realisateur" "draft, not yet bashified"
.SH NAME
consigne \- the vault-consign step of PROSE-REAPING.md
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B consigne
--from <project> --file <path> [--file <path> ...] -m <message-file> [--apply]
.br
.B consigne
--from <project> --diff <treeish> -m <message-file> [--apply]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Copies the named files out of a project repo
(\fI$HOME/Documents/Projects/<project>\fR) into the Obsidian vault
(\fI$HOME/ecosystem1/ecosystem1/<project>/\fR) and commits them there with a
caller-supplied message in the vault's established "consign: ..." convention.
Dry run by default; \fB\-\-apply\fR is required to actually copy and commit.
.PP
Never pushes. No code path in the implementation runs
.B git push
against the vault remote -- see PROSE-REAPING.md for why (Zach's IP/licensing
note, standing until ethics guards around IP exist).
.PP
This tool does not decide WHAT is narrative. PROSE-REAPING.md's per-paragraph
criterion is a judgement call for a human or an agent; this is the mechanical
back half once that judgement has produced a drafted vault file and a
commit message.
.SH STATUS
DRAFT. Ships today as a plain script at \fBbin/consigne.sh\fR, not yet run
through the bashify pipeline into a VERB_NAME-based verb -- see the PR that
introduced it for what graduation needs (subcommand split if warranted,
DEPENDS.tsv rows, a bashified branch, CONTRACT.md entry).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 ok (dry run completed, or commit made); 2 usage; 4 GAP (missing source or
vault repo, or the source project is BUSY); 5 BROKEN (copy or git operation
failed after files were already touched).
